v 3
d peerpick: choose a comparison group for one unit and check how much the choice matters
d
d peerpick builds a comparison group (peers) for one unit -- a county,
d a city, a school, a hospital, a firm, a region, a country -- from a
d dataset of candidates: nearest
d neighbours by Mahalanobis or standardized Euclidean distance, coarsened
d cells, typology cells, propensity scores, predicted values, k-means
d clusters, entropy balancing, a hand-picked list, trajectory distance on
d a panel, or synthetic-control weights.  Every method leaves the same
d things behind: a flag, a weight, a distance, a rank, a balance table,
d and the gap on an outcome with an interval.
d
d Three subcommands replay the call to check the choice: a specification
d curve over k, distance, factors, and strata; placebo gaps with every
d unit as the focal; and leave-one-out stability over comparison units
d and factors.
d
d Base Stata and Mata, no dependencies.  Example data: Texas counties
d (ACS, PLACES, RUCC), a SAIPE county poverty panel, and a FRED state
d panel.  An in-browser simulator (one offline HTML file) lets you make
d the same choices by hand and watch the group and the gap change.
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Author: Eric Booth
d Support: email eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261020
f src/peerpick.ado
f src/peerpick.sthlp
f data/tx_counties.dta
f data/tx_county_panel.dta
f data/us_states.dta
f examples/peerpick_examples.do
f tests/test01_methods.do
f tests/test02_panel_subcommands.do
f simulator/peer_simulator.html
